        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "B3ABt",
          "name": "verdict",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "fill": "$background-tertiary",
          "cornerRadius": 4,
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "padding": 12,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "U2xX5",
              "name": "h",
              "fill": "$text-primary",
              "content": "Recommendation: Candidate B (hybrid)",
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 12,
              "fontWeight": "600"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "j2NKAe",
              "name": "p",
              "fill": "$text-tertiary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Category arrives through two channels at once (pastel fill AND glyph), which strengthens the ratified never-color-alone rule instead of trading against it.",
              "lineHeight": 1.35,
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "KoDen",
              "name": "p",
              "fill": "$text-tertiary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Experts get the Houdini vocabulary that matters for dense-graph scanning: wing flags, per-type glyphs, grey type labels, teal descriptions.",
              "lineHeight": 1.35,
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "tL1Ow",
              "name": "p",
              "fill": "$text-tertiary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "The pastel affordance that serves the novice and intermediate personas survives untouched, as does every shipped category semantic.",
              "lineHeight": 1.35,
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "T2rHFZ",
              "name": "p",
              "fill": "$text-tertiary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "A is the strongest pure-Houdini statement but deletes the ratified pastel channel; because fills are tokens, an A-style neutral skin can ship later as a theme variant with zero structural change.",
              "lineHeight": 1.35,
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "g0SNpi",
              "name": "p",
              "fill": "$text-tertiary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "C is the cheapest but leaves the node face without per-type identity, under-serving the technical north star.",
              "lineHeight": 1.35,
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
