              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "G4bXl",
                  "name": "id",
                  "fill": "$accent-primary",
                  "content": "D-3",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
                  "fontSize": 12,
                  "fontWeight": "700"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "l1mlG",
                  "name": "k",
                  "fill": "$warn-badge",
                  "content": "AMENDED",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
                  "fontSize": 8,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "FJxss",
              "name": "b",
              "fill": "$text-tertiary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Display flag = halo disc behind the node (#58a6ff) AND the right wing tab. The disc is the at-a-distance cue, the wing is the click target. This matters more in Solarxy than in Houdini: there is no OUT node type, the display terminal is a graph-level flag (Subflow::active_output), so any node can hold it and the halo is the only way to see the graph's output from across the canvas.",
              "lineHeight": 1.45,
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "z3hVbZ",
          "name": "dec D-4",
          "width": 712,
          "gap": 12,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "NX3MD",
              "name": "lc",
              "width": 70,
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 3,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "ElAFU",
                  "name": "id",
                  "fill": "$accent-primary",
                  "content": "D-4",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
                  "fontSize": 12,
                  "fontWeight": "700"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "bN5CV",
                  "name": "k",
                  "fill": "$warn-badge",
                  "content": "AMENDED",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
                  "fontSize": 8,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "rPrSP",
              "name": "b",
              "fill": "$text-tertiary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Body 112 x 28 (4:1, the Houdini ratio) for every silhouette; a fixed layout box keeps the handle axis and the wires invariant across shapes. Glyph 16px on a 20px light chip at the body centre, on the handle axis. Wings: visual 10px, hit area 18x54. Handles float clear of the body (3px gap) and keep DataType colour + shape - Houdini's plain grey dots would destroy that ratified channel. Terminal, branch and light carry no wings. REVISED 2026-08-06 (06-10, D-26/D-27): the box is 112 x 32 and it is a true layout box: every role occupies it, a sized-down body centres inside it (the root roles are one 96x28 fixture pill), and only the gather dome rides above it. The glyph inks directly on the body, no plate. Wings ride the bodies, revealed on hover, bypass left; the right wing carries display in subflows and the visible param at root, the floating root eye is retired, and each wing renders only where the registry declares its fact.",
              "lineHeight": 1.45,
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "zOD86",
          "name": "dec D-7",
          "width": 712,
          "gap": 12,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "v5WLu7",
              "name": "lc",
              "width": 70,
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 3,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "GuVmd",
                  "name": "id",
                  "fill": "$accent-primary",
                  "content": "D-7",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
                  "fontSize": 12,
                  "fontWeight": "700"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "a6eJR",
                  "name": "k",
                  "fill": "$warn-badge",
                  "content": "AMENDED",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
                  "fontSize": 8,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "WkE7a",
              "name": "b",
              "fill": "$text-tertiary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Radial: 6 uniform wedges with north and south left open for the wires. Rename is the 6th action and reuses the existing F2 binding, so no new engine command. Inner radius must exceed the node's half-diagonal, or the node punches through the ring (the round-1 bug).",
              "lineHeight": 1.45,
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "RGiT4",
          "name": "dec D-10",
          "width": 712,
          "gap": 12,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "uI3WA",
              "name": "lc",
              "width": 70,
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 3,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "HupKV",
                  "name": "id",
                  "fill": "$accent-primary",
                  "content": "D-10",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
                  "fontSize": 12,
                  "fontWeight": "700"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "ADsO9",
                  "name": "k",
                  "fill": "$connection-line-valid",
                  "content": "NEW",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
                  "fontSize": 8,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "I6u6x2",
              "name": "b",
              "fill": "$text-tertiary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Silhouette = topological role, fill = category, glyph = type. Eight shapes plus the container square and note sticky, all derived from the RegistrySnapshot (06-06), never a per-type table. REVISED: source is no longer a shape - Houdini does not distinguish generators from filters by outline either, and the absent input handle already says it. The dome is the VARIADIC marker and rides both merge and switch, exactly as the reference does. switch is a flattened hexagon, null a bold donut, validate a top-heavy trapezoid, import_image a folded-corner page (it takes the page because the Houdini-faithful hexagon for switch collides with it; the round-2 hexagon-matches-the-Image-handle tie-in is what gives).",
              "lineHeight": 1.45,
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "NtMum",
          "name": "dec D-11",
          "width": 712,
          "gap": 12,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "h0yfeo",
              "name": "lc",
              "width": 70,
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 3,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "U2jUUc",
                  "name": "id",
                  "fill": "$accent-primary",
                  "content": "D-11",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
                  "fontSize": 12,
                  "fontWeight": "700"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "N2rQ8",
                  "name": "k",
                  "fill": "$connection-line-valid",
                  "content": "NEW",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
                  "fontSize": 8,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "R0dTur",
              "name": "b",
              "fill": "$text-tertiary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Status moves off the node body into a glyph row under the name, Houdini-style, plus a blue param-preview line sourced from the existing nodeInfoLine. The body carries only the glyph and wings; the selection ring, display halo and cook spinner all sit outside it. This structurally prevents the badge collisions found in round 1.",
              "lineHeight": 1.45,
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "vJWoH",
          "name": "dec D-12",
          "width": 712,
          "gap": 12,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "XB7MO",
              "name": "lc",
              "width": 70,
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 3,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "VgVYv",
                  "name": "id",
                  "fill": "$accent-primary",
                  "content": "D-12",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
                  "fontSize": 12,
                  "fontWeight": "700"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "y0piOb",
                  "name": "k",
                  "fill": "$connection-line-valid",
                  "content": "NEW",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
                  "fontSize": 8,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "UOtAR",
              "name": "b",
              "fill": "$text-tertiary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Instrument body treatment. Every silhouette carries vertical segmentation slots (~22px pitch), the glyph on a light chip, and top-down shading. This is the single biggest reason a Houdini node reads as a Houdini node, and it costs almost nothing to implement: one repeating gradient for the slots and one inner element for the chip. Authored here as a shader fill (slots.glsl) layered over the category token, so the pastel still drives the colour.",
              "lineHeight": 1.45,
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
