      "fill": "$background-primary",
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": 18,
      "padding": 24,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "BPMku",
          "name": "Sheet title",
          "fill": "$text-primary",
          "content": "Roadmap nav collapse (0.8.2)",
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 18,
          "fontWeight": "600"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "a575J",
          "name": "cap",
          "fill": "$text-tertiary",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 900,
          "content": "The roadmap page's ten section links are in-page navigation for a very long document, so hiding them below a breakpoint, the landing page's answer, would remove the only way to move around the page exactly where it matters most. Below 860px, the page's largest existing layout threshold, the link row collapses into one disclosure control that is labelled by the section currently in view and opens the full section list as a panel. This is the first interactive disclosure on the public pages: it defines the house pattern and lives in the shared chrome as a helper that collapses only when a nav carries more links than fit, so the references page with its three static links never changes. Artboard colours are the editorial tokens from the public stylesheet, quoted as literals because the public pages deliberately do not use the app token set.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 11,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
